---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/postscript-vs-smsbump";
const title = "Postscript vs retired SMSBump: Shopify SMS replacement guide";
const desc = "SMSBump/Yotpo SMS is decommissioned. Evaluate Postscript against retained permissions, sender recovery and loyalty-message dependencies.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I start a new SMSBump program?",
    "answer": "No. The Yotpo SMS lifecycle notice says the application is decommissioned and its dashboard and background services are inactive. An old SMSBump comparison is historical context, not a current buying option."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a Yotpo Loyalty subscription keep SMSBump running?",
    "answer": "Do not infer that. Continuing Reviews or Loyalty functionality must be inventoried separately from the retired SMS product. Confirm the supported replacement connection and who sends each message."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Postscript a guaranteed migration destination?",
    "answer": "No. Evaluate its current account eligibility, sender-transfer process, supported data imports and required integrations. A historical contact list does not prove permission or recover old message queues."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
<header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Shopify decision guide</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">{desc}</p></header>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<p><em>Scope checked November 25, 2026. Supplier documentation supports product scope, not comparative performance. Exercises below are proposed and unperformed.</em></p>
<h2>SMSBump is a retired-product search, not a bundle offer</h2>
<p>The <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo SMS lifecycle notice</a> says the application is decommissioned and that its dashboard and background services are inactive. Yotpo’s <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">migration announcement</a> scheduled Email/SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Do not run a new SMSBump trial or price a renewed SMS bundle from an old comparison. The current job is to identify the store’s live sender and any unresolved records from its former program.</p>
<h2>Find the phone program before importing a list</h2>
<p>Locate retained exports, agency handover records and the account that currently owns the sending number. Separate subscribers with documented phone permission from phone numbers collected for delivery or support. Preserve source, timestamp and opt-out evidence where available; do not turn missing evidence into an affirmative subscription. Ask the former provider about any remaining recovery path rather than promising dashboard access after decommissioning. Keep an explicit record of unrecoverable history.</p>
<h2>Evaluate Postscript as a replacement sender</h2>
<p><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/launch">Postscript’s current product page</a> describes SMS and announces Email with a waitlist link. Establish the SMS scope needed first: subscriber acquisition, cart messages, campaign targeting and reply handling. If email consolidation is also proposed, confirm eligibility independently. Neither the product announcement nor the old SMSBump brand establishes automatic transfer of senders, consent records or flow definitions. Request a migration mapping for the actual retained records.</p>
<h2>Separate sender continuity from customer identity</h2>
<p>A Shopify customer ID, a phone number and a sending number serve different jobs. Reconcile duplicate customer records without overwriting opt-outs, then confirm the supported path and timing for any sender transfer with the relevant providers. Do not assume an old branded sender can be reused immediately. Keep the operational owner, dependencies and fallback channel documented so a transfer gap does not trigger an unapproved import or duplicate program.</p>
<h2>Loyalty messages need fresh ownership</h2>
<p>Continuing Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty should be evaluated on their own current role. Inventory tier announcements, points reminders, review invitations and promotional offers separately. For a Postscript replacement, obtain the supported integration and exact available events and fields; do not assume a native loyalty connection or prescribe middleware without checking it. If a live balance is unavailable, avoid copy asserting an exact balance. A loyalty-related message is not automatically exempt from marketing permission requirements.</p>
<h2>Proposed rehearsal: old keyword meets a new sender</h2>
<p>This is an unperformed exercise for the replacement program. Inventory old packaging, QR codes, popup forms and keyword landing pages that still mention the former SMS sender. With approved test identities, check where each entry point leads and how it records permission. Update or retire dead entry points before acquisition resumes. Then test an opt-out and a reply needing human support in the intended sender. An imported list alone cannot validate these physical and digital acquisition paths.</p>
<h2>Rebuild journeys without reviving obsolete intent</h2>
<p>Recreate welcome from eligible new signups, not from the import timestamp of every historical contact. For cart recovery, check that archived checkouts do not enter as fresh abandonments. For post-purchase, distinguish product education from review requests already owned elsewhere. For winback, use retained purchase history only where it is trustworthy. Proposed tests should include a completed purchase before a queued reminder and an opted-out customer appearing in a later import. Keep sending disabled until exclusions and exits behave as intended.</p>
<h2>Price recovery and operation separately</h2>
<p>Use a current replacement quote for retained eligible subscribers, sending regions, normal and peak message segments, required support and integration work. Keep continuing Reviews/Loyalty charges outside the retired SMS comparison. Track record recovery, template rebuilding and old acquisition-material updates as transition work. Historical SMSBump prices and invented revenue-share breakpoints cannot establish current value. Choose Postscript only if the required program is supported and staffed; keep missing records, number transfer and integration gaps explicit rather than calling a contact import a complete migration.</p>
</article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/recart-vs-postscript">Recart vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs SMSBump FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
